  {
   "id": "VZLocuY6AgAJ",
   "from": "Dominique Cirkel",
   "author": "a6bda949fbb66786",
   "date": "2017-06-27T09:42:55Z",
   "subject": "Re: [simmer-devel] Using now(env) in mclapply{} and wrap()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Oh wow, such a simple solution. I can&#39;t believe I didnt think of that. </div><div><br></div><div>Anyways: Thanks so much, it works fine now!</div><div><br><br>Op maandag 26 juni 2017 17:40:21 UTC+2 schreef Iñaki Úcar:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Hi Dominique,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">My question\r\nhere is twofold: </font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">\r\n\r\n</font><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc;direction:ltr\"><li style=\"font-style:normal\"><p style=\"font-style:normal;margin-top:0cm;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Is\r\nthere a way in which I can investigate the queue of only the new patients without\r\nthe use of now()? (I’ve tried join(), without success)</font></span></p></li></ul></div></div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Yes, there is. You just need to extract the arrivals per resource. This data frame contains all access to resources. Given that you are interested in the first-timers, you need to keep the first appearance of each person, filtering out everything else. In dplyr terms,</p>\r\n<pre style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;line-height:1.2em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em\"><code style=\"background:rgb(248,248,248);margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0.5em;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);color:rgb(51,51,51);overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:0.85em;display:block!important;white-space:pre\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">library</span>(dplyr)\r\n\r\nwaiting_time &lt;- get_mon_arrivals(env, per_resource=<span>TRUE</span>) %&gt;%\r\n  group_by(replication, name) %&gt;%\r\n  slice(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>) %&gt;%\r\n  transmute(waiting_time = end_time - start_time - activity_time)\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><ul style=\"list-style-type:disc;direction:ltr\"><li style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal\"><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;margin-top:0cm;margin-bottom:10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Can\r\nI use mclapply and now() somehow at the same time?</font></span></p></li></ul></div></div></blockquote><p></p></div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Given my first answer, you don’t need <code style=\"margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:0.85em;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">now()</code> anymore, but yes, you can. You just need to enclose your whole simulation inside the function you pass to <code style=\"margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:0.85em;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">mclapply</code>, including the trajectory. Why? Because it is calling <code style=\"margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:0.85em;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">now(env)</code>, so that the <code style=\"margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:0.85em;display:inline;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">env</code> should be defined in the same level as the trajectory itself. For instance:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;line-height:1.2em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em\"><code style=\"background:rgb(248,248,248);margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0.5em;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);color:rgb(51,51,51);overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:0.85em;display:block!important;white-space:pre\">my_simulation &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>(i) {\r\n  patientpath &lt;- trajectory(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;Patients&#39; path&quot;</span>)  %&gt;%\r\n    set_attribute(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;Starttime&quot;</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">function</span>() now(env)) %&gt;%\r\n    <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">...</span>\r\n\r\n  env &lt;- simmer() %&gt;% \r\n    add_resource(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;doctor&quot;</span>, capacity = <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">2</span>) %&gt;%\r\n    add_generator(<span style=\"color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;person&quot;</span>, patientpath, at(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">0</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">10</span>), mon = <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">2</span>) \r\n\r\n  env %&gt;% \r\n    run(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">50</span>) %&gt;%\r\n    wrap()\r\n}\r\n\r\nenvs &lt;- mclapply(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">100</span>, my_simulation)\r\n</code></pre>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Regards,</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGkgRG9taW5pcXVlLDxkaXYgY2xhc3M9ImdtYWlsX2V4dHJhIj4